      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey i keep getting this error in my reconcil report macro and cant figure out why. \n\nrun-time error '1004': application-defined or object-defined error\n\nhere is the part that crashes:\n\nSub MonthlyRecon()\n    Dim ws As Worksheet\n    Set ws = ThisWorkbook.Sheets(\"Recon_Final\")\n    \n    ws.Range(\"A1:Z1\").Value = \"Month-End Report\"\n    \n    For i = 2 To 100\n        If ws.Cells(i, 1).Value <> \"\" Then\n            ws.Range(\"B\" & i).Value = ws.Cells(i, 1).Value * 1.05\n        End If\n    Next i\n    \n    ws.Activate\n    ws.Range(\"A1\").Select\nEnd Sub",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The Index out of range error often occurs because the range \"B\" & i in the macro does not correctly handle cases where there may be empty cells before column B starts. Adjust the range to account for empty cells in the column. Here is the modified code:\n\nSub MonthlyRecon()\n    Dim ws As Worksheet\n    Set ws = ThisWorkbook.Sheets(\"Recon_Final\")\n    \n    ws.Range(\"A1:Z1\").Value = \"Month-End Report\"\n    \n    For i = 2 To ws.Cells(ws.Rows.Count, 1).End(xlUp).Row\n        If ws.Cells(i, 1).Value <> \"\" Then\n            ws.Cells(i, 2).Value = ws.Cells(i, 1).Value * 1.05\n        End If\n    Next i\n    \n    ws.Activate\n    ws.Range(\"A1\").Select\nEnd Sub\n\nLet me know if this fixes the issue!",
